# Allowlisted defaults-parity divergences (hack/check-defaults-parity.py).
#
# One path pattern per line; `#` starts a comment and blank lines are ignored.
# A pattern matches the exact path and any path below it. Every entry here is a
# deliberate, pre-existing divergence between the loader defaults
# (templates/loader/_defaults.tpl) and the defaults documented in values.yaml.
# Keep this list tiny — anything not listed fails `make check-defaults-parity`.
#
# Loader-only: consumer-facing derived key, set to "" so the loader can tell
# "consumer set it" apart from "we derived it"; documented in the README
# (Object Buckets -> PostgreSQL backups), intentionally absent from values.yaml.
postgres.backup.objectStore.bucketRef
# Values-only: the CNPG class templates default these label maps themselves
# (see templates/classes/_cnpg-podmonitor.tpl and _cnpg-alerts.tpl);
# values.yaml documents the kube-prometheus-stack-usable default.
postgres.monitoring.podMonitorLabels
postgres.monitoring.prometheusRuleLabels
# Values-only: consumer override keys that default to empty and are read with
# `default ""` (mutually exclusive S3 path vs existing PVC); documented in
# values.yaml, no loader default needed.
dragonfly.snapshot.dir
dragonfly.snapshot.existingPersistentVolumeClaimName
